   128	   * convention two concurrent writers can silently violate. Roots, not live
   129	   * heads: this function inserts the successor before stamping the
   130	   * predecessor's `superseded_by`, so both are briefly live and a live-head
   131	   * index would reject every ordinary supersede. Uniqueness is declared per
   132	   * namespace on purpose: `entity_identities` enforces one blanket index across
   133	   * every namespace and has carried a dead `uniquePerOrg` knob ever since.
   134	   *
   135	   * Rows with no stable identity (messages, notes, tombstones, change audits)
   136	   * leave this unset — there is no "current version of" a one-shot event.
   137	   */
   138	  identity?: { ns: string; key: string } | null;
   139	
   140	  /** Audit */
   141	  createdBy?: string | null;
   142	  clientId?: string | null;
   143	}
